**How to implement.** AT-1 proves the read path on the committed kit (001 §Q 'Open: the test then opens the COMMITTED kit read-only through the real folder `KitProxy`, against an EMPTY library database, and runs its study from there. This proves the read path: the library snapshot, the relative paths and hashes, and the data import. A test never writes into `data/`'; .spec-md §3.12 'A read-only open writes nothing'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S12.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs`: `emptyLibraryAppContext (owner : FolderName) : AppContext`, with a one-line doc citing 001 §Q 'Open', is `AppContext.create` over `testLocations owner` (step 83) whose shipped catalogue folder is a fresh, empty folder under the test output, so the start-up import finds no catalogue, logs its refusal and leaves the SQLite `:memory:` library empty (step 100). (2) The fact `the committed optics-mueller kit opens read-only against an empty library, writes nothing, and its study reproduces the reference reconstruction` in `KitAcceptanceTests`: before anything, the committed folder's relative paths and bytes are recorded. Over `emptyLibraryAppContext (FolderName "KitAcceptanceTests")`, a start screen built as step 421 builds one sends `OpenKitReadOnly` of the committed folder (step 177), and the kit is opened read-only through `KitProxy.create`'s `readOnlyView` (step 131); the window model is `TestAppScope.inverseModelOver` of the context and the opened kit. Then: the context's item-model store and live library list no entry, while every one of the nine items resolves its model through the kit's snapshots (`model.tryItemModelChoice`, steps 142, 222, 263); the opened kit holds the 53 experiments, the 42 setups, the 9 items, the study and its two fit runs; every experiment's attachment status is unchanged at its recorded hash (`attachmentStatus`, step 134) and its data loads through the Phone ROI CSV profile (`readMapped`, step 305) to its group's points; `assertReferenceInstruments model.kitItems` holds (step 427). (3) The study runs from there through the study engine itself, because a fit run's write is refused under a read-only kit (steps 185, 413): `StudyFitParam.runFit` (step 391) of `{ study = QZ-LR; stage = ObjectStage; calibrationUse = CalibrationHeldFixed }` under `UnwatchedIterations` (step 380), the parameter being `model.studyForwardContext`, a clock fixed at 2026-05-31T12:03:00Z, the solver and deviates `StudyFitEnvironment.create` composes (step 393) and `model.kitFitRuns`, answers `Ok run` with `LinearStudyEngine`, and `assertReferenceObjects run` holds (step 427). Afterwards the committed folder's relative paths and bytes equal the recorded ones: nothing was written, no lock, stamp, snapshot or cache (.spec-md §3.12). No product code changes. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the read path lands, the committed kit MUST open read-only against an empty library, resolve every item model from its snapshots, load every attachment at its hash, reproduce the published instruments and, through `StudyFitParam.runFit`, the reference matrices and product-check ratio within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol`, and leave every file of the committed folder unchanged; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `the committed optics-mueller kit opens read-only against an empty library, writes nothing, and its study reproduces the reference reconstruction`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.
